<h1 class="ct-art-title">VERRA: Building a Skincare Identity Around Simplicity</h1>
<p class="ct-art-dek">A brand identity for a skincare brand built on considered formulations and uncomplicated everyday care, where premium doesn't have to mean excessive.</p>
<div class="ct-art-meta"><img alt="" src="/img/team-subomi.webp"/><span>Olasubomi Archibong</span><span class="dot"></span><span>3 min read</span></div>
</div>
<img alt="VERRA brand identity: wordmark, palette, bottles, a tote bag and a sweatshirt in deep forest green" class="ct-art-cover" src="/img/verra-overview.webp"/>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section ct-art-body">
<div class="container w-layout-blockcontainer">
<div class="ct-art-col">
<p class="ct-art-lead">In skincare, the product is only part of the experience. Before someone reads an ingredient list, tries a formulation or adds something to their routine, they encounter the brand.</p>
<p>Its name. Its packaging. Its visual identity. The impression it creates.</p>
<p>For VERRA, the opportunity was to build an identity that reflected the thinking behind the products: considered formulations, quality ingredients and uncomplicated everyday skincare.</p>
<p>The challenge was to translate that philosophy into a visual language that felt premium and distinctive without becoming excessive.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="VERRA wordmark above product photography, the full colour palette and the Monument Extended and Inter typefaces" loading="lazy" src="/img/verra-identity.webp"/><figcaption>Care, in its purest form: the wordmark, palette and type system together.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>The thinking behind the brand</h2>
<p>Skincare branding often leans heavily on familiar visual cues. But a brand built around simplicity and considered formulations needs an identity that communicates those qualities without feeling generic.</p>
<p>For VERRA, we wanted to find a balance between restraint and character.</p>
<p>The identity needed to feel confident but not loud, elegant without being overly decorative, and minimal without losing its personality.</p>
<p>Rather than adding visual elements for the sake of making the brand look more elaborate, we focused on creating a system where every element had a reason to be there.</p>
<h2>Bringing the identity to life</h2>
<p>We approached the visual identity as a connected brand experience.</p>
<h3>Typography</h3>
<p>The typography establishes the brand's personality. It needed to feel refined and contemporary while remaining clear and recognisable.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="VERRA typography sheet: Monument Extended for headlines, Inter for body copy, wordmark clear space and signature colours" loading="lazy" src="/img/verra-typography.webp"/><figcaption>Monument Extended for headlines and display, Inter for everyday communication.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>Colour palette</h3>
<p>The palette supports the brand's understated direction, creating a visual foundation that feels considered rather than overly decorative.</p>
<h3>Packaging</h3>
<p>Packaging was an important part of translating the brand's philosophy into something tangible. The direction needed to feel consistent with the product experience: uncomplicated, intentional and premium.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="VERRA packaging: a pump bottle and tube in deep forest green, a jar on a stone plinth and the label design" loading="lazy" src="/img/verra-packaging-v2.webp"/><figcaption>Bottles, jars and label designs.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>The wider visual language</h3>
<p>Beyond individual design elements, the aim was to create cohesion. The logo, typography, colours and packaging needed to feel like parts of the same brand, not separate creative decisions.</p>
<h2>The result: simplicity with a point of view</h2>
<p>VERRA's identity is built around a simple idea: <b>premium doesn't have to mean excessive.</b></p>
<p>The result is a visual direction that communicates quality and confidence through considered choices rather than unnecessary complexity.</p>
<p>It gives the brand a recognisable presence while staying true to the philosophy behind its products.</p>
<p>For us, that's what thoughtful brand identity should do. It should make a business recognisable, communicate what it stands for and create a consistent experience wherever people encounter it.</p>
<blockquote class="ct-art-quote">VERRA is a reminder that sometimes the strongest creative decisions are the ones you make with intention.</blockquote>
<p>Brand identity by Colorteam.</p>
